From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jianfeng Liu <Jianfeng.Liu@cixtech.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 35/92] ASoC: cix: fix DP audio codec device lookup

cix_acpi_dp_audio_get_codec_name() used device_find_any_child() on the
DP platform device to find the HDMI codec child.  The PM core also
parents a "wakeup<N>" wakeup-source stats device to the same device,
and device_find_any_child() may return that one instead, producing a
bogus codec name that the card can never bind to (-EPROBE_DEFER
forever).

Match the codec child by its HDMI_CODEC_DRV_NAME name prefix instead.

Signed-off-by: Jianfeng Liu <Jianfeng.Liu@cixtech.com>
---
 sound/soc/cix/card-utils.c | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/cix/card-utils.c b/sound/soc/cix/card-utils.c
index 2f202e3e9..c19e6dc8f 100644
--- a/sound/soc/cix/card-utils.c
+++ b/sound/soc/cix/card-utils.c
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 #include <linux/regmap.h>
 #include <linux/version.h>
 #include "card-utils.h"
+#include <sound/hdmi-codec.h>
 #include <sound/jack.h>
 
 #define SKY1_AUDSS_CRU_INFO_MCLK		0x70
@@ -881,6 +882,19 @@ static const char *cix_acpi_dp_audio_get_cpu_name(int idx)
 	return dev_name(&adev->dev);
 }
 
+static int cix_dp_audio_codec_match(struct device *dev, const void *data)
+{
+	/* The DP DRM driver registers the HDMI codec as a child platform
+	 * device named "hdmi-audio-codec.<id>.auto" (HDMI_CODEC_DRV_NAME with
+	 * an auto-allocated id). Match it by name prefix instead of grabbing
+	 * an arbitrary child: the PM core also parents a "wakeup<N>" wakeup
+	 * source stats device to the DP platform device, and device_find_any
+	 * _child() may return that one, producing a bogus codec name that the
+	 * card can never bind (-EPROBE_DEFER forever).
+	 */
+	return strstarts(dev_name(dev), HDMI_CODEC_DRV_NAME);
+}
+
 static const char *cix_acpi_dp_audio_get_codec_name(int idx)
 {
 	struct acpi_device *adev;
@@ -902,7 +916,7 @@ static const char *cix_acpi_dp_audio_get_codec_name(int idx)
 	if (!dev)
 		return NULL;
 
-	dpdev = device_find_any_child(dev);
+	dpdev = device_find_child(dev, NULL, cix_dp_audio_codec_match);
 	if (!dpdev)
 		return NULL;
 
